WOW-BG3 vmangos patch 0017: held creatures walk on at once when they are let go.

Thaw (a release without evade: BG3's turn-based mode ended, or a fight let a mob go) now resets a
waypoint or random movement generator. The hold's StopMoving made the waypoint generator wait
STOP_TIME_FOR_PLAYER (30 s), as for a creature a player talks to, so every patrol stood half a
minute after turn-based mode (a playtest report).

diff --git a/src/game/WowBg3Fights.cpp b/src/game/WowBg3Fights.cpp
index 13af21a..742c7ff 100644
--- a/src/game/WowBg3Fights.cpp
+++ b/src/game/WowBg3Fights.cpp
@@ -34,6 +34,7 @@
 #include "GridNotifiersImpl.h"
 #include "Creature.h"
 #include "CreatureAI.h"
+#include "MovementGenerator.h"                       // 0017: Thaw resets a patrol
 #include "Log.h"
 #include "Map.h"
 #include "MapManager.h"
@@ -435,7 +436,19 @@ namespace
             }
         }
         else
+        {
             c->UpdateLeashExtensionTime();
+            // 0017: a patrol or a wanderer goes on at once. The hold stopped it (StopMoving), and the
+            // waypoint generator takes a stopped creature for one a player is talking to: it waits
+            // STOP_TIME_FOR_PLAYER (30 s) before it walks again, so after BG3's turn-based mode
+            // every walking NPC stood half a minute. Reset starts the next leg now.
+            if (!c->IsInCombat())
+            {
+                MovementGeneratorType const t = c->GetMotionMaster()->GetCurrentMovementGeneratorType();
+                if (t == WAYPOINT_MOTION_TYPE || t == RANDOM_MOTION_TYPE)
+                    const_cast<MovementGenerator*>(c->GetMotionMaster()->GetCurrent())->Reset(*c);
+            }
+        }
     }
 
     // Anyone on the threat list who is not this player, their pet or their group.
